  "note": "Complete principal U-shaped Bellevue Palace exterior:main front/rear range,two perpendicular three-level wings,hipped wing-end pavilions and attached southwest low service link. Include dark pitched tiled roofscape,chimneys/rooflights,front giant pilasters/triangular pediment/clock/original statues,rectangular and oval glazed windows,central doorway/steps and rear doorway/terrace. Separate oval modern office,guardhouse,wider park,walls,flags,furniture and optical interiors excluded. Native main10m,side11m and end/link8m tags are generalized;source original photo-proportional cornice/roof/level envelopes are not surveyed. Main floor2.2m above32m approximate datum;main eave15.2m/ridge22.2m,pediment20.2m/central statue22.45m;wings eave14.4m/ridge20.4m,low link7.2m/10.5m. Variable-depth structural foundations and original front/rear grade-adapter steps meet the unchanged global field;no flattening. +X northeast toward Spree-side wing,-X southwest toward low service link;+Z southeast open entrance court,-Z northwest rear garden;+Y up."
